NAME
       fstrim - tell the storage which blocks of a file system are unused

SYNOPSIS
       fstrim [-a] [-v] [MOUNTPOINT]

DESCRIPTION
       On SSDs and thin-provisioned storage it helps to tell the device which
       blocks hold no data any more, so it can reuse them. fstrim does that
       for a mounted file system. RHEL has a weekly fstrim.timer that can do
       it for every file system (systemctl enable --now fstrim.timer).

OPTIONS
       -a, --all
              Trim every mounted file system that supports it.

       -v, --verbose
              Print how much was trimmed.

EXAMPLES
           fstrim -v /

SEE ALSO
       mount(8), systemctl(1)
